# Language

## Workshop app (English)

All user-visible strings in the React app use **English**:

- Header, section labels, placeholders, loading/error text
- `index.html` `lang="en"`

Do not add Chinese (or other) UI copy to workshop chrome unless the user explicitly changes this rule.

## 16:9 stage

- Stage markup uses `src/styles/stage.css` tokens only — no shadcn on the canvas.
- **Slide content** (`weeks/YYYY-MM-DD.json`: titles, bullets, tables) is user-authored weekly-report copy; it may be English, Chinese, or mixed. Do not force English on week files when editing report content.

## Code

- **Comments**: Traditional Chinese; explain why, not what.
- **Strings and errors in code**: English.

## Docs

- `README.md` and `docs/agents/*`: English.
- `.scratch/` tickets and spec: English (existing convention).
